<title>USA: Fed sets money supply growth targets for 1997.</title>
<headline>Fed sets money supply growth targets for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following ranges for growth of monetary and credit aggregates were set by the Federal Reserve's Federal Open Market Committee.</p>
<p>				(Percent change Q4 to Q4)</p>
<p>			Actual	     Target</p>
<p>			 1996		 1997</p>
<p>   M2		  4.6	     1.0 to 5.0</p>
<p>   M3		  6.9	     2.0 to 6.0</p>
<p>   Debt		5.3	     3.0 to 7.0</p>
<p>(The Fed in July, 1996, set provisional targets of 1.0 to 5.0 pct for M2, 2.0 to 6.0 pct for M3 and 3.0 to 7.0 pct for debt)</p>
</text>
